# What the second analyser does not read, and the whole of it.
#
# This file exists because the tool has a default list when there is none, and
# that list skips tests/ and fixtures/ among others. Under it, the scan of this
# repository read zero of the three fixture files that prove the rules bite and
# printed a green summary saying so. A gate that is green because it read nothing
# is the failure the fixtures exist against, so the default is replaced here
# rather than argued with.
#
# The file name is the tool's, which is Opengrep's ancestor's rather than
# Opengrep's own. The name is what the binary looks for; renaming it would mean
# the list below silently stops applying and the default comes back.
#
# tools/opengrep/rules.yml holds the rules, and .github/workflows/second-analyser.yml
# is where the scan runs. What the gate excludes beyond this list is one path
# given on the command line there, the fixtures, which the proof job scans on its
# own instead.

# Installed dependencies. Not this repository's code, and scanning them would
# report somebody else's tree as this project's findings.
node_modules/
